
  12 synthetic fields of 900 px, 12 cells each
  radius 2.5-8.0 um = 8.8-28.1 px   peak phase 0.8-3.0 rad
  calibration: pitch 0.284871 um, pixel area 0.081151 um^2, 4.300915e-02 pg per rad-pixel
  instance labelling: watershed, watershed distance 15 px

=== pipeline error against exact ground truth ===
  cells placed 144   measured 134   paired 134
  area  signed  mean +0.0395%   median +0.0330%   p95 |.| 0.6787%
  mass  signed  mean +0.0074%   median +0.0084%   p95 |.| 0.1346%
  field-summed mass  mean -1.6655%   median -2.0152%

  10 of 144 cells were never measured. min_cell_area_um2 = 30.0 um^2 rejects anything below 3.09 um of radius,
  and the synthesised radii start at 2.50 um. That is the whole of the gap between a per-cell error of 0.04%
  and a field-summed error of -1.67%: the filter discards small cells, so the
  TOTAL mass of a field is biased low by that much while every cell it keeps is exact.
  Report the filter's cost whenever a field total or a population mean is reported.

     radius (um)  cells    |dA/A|    |dm/m|
    3.10-4.21        34   0.4583%   0.0887%
    4.21-5.78        33   0.2458%   0.0401%
    5.78-6.80        33   0.1236%   0.0188%
    6.80-7.95        34   0.1483%   0.0139%

=== the loss term against the analytic answer, 6 cells of 6.0 um radius ===
  exact prediction            0.000e+00   (must be 0)
  phase scaled by 1.07        0.070000   (must be 0.070000)
  area term, exact foreground 0.000e+00   (must be 0)

  -> the measurement pipeline reproduces exact ground truth to 0.04% in dry
     mass on the cells it keeps, and the loss term returns the analytic
     relative error. That 0.04% is the FLOOR under every PER-CELL
     measurement error this project reports: a measured error of 4% is
     99x the floor, so it is model error and not pipeline error. The
     floor grows for small cells -- see the table by radius.

     But the FIELD TOTAL has a separate and much larger bias, -1.67%,
     entirely from the area filter discarding small cells. The two floors
     are different numbers for different claims: quote 0.04% for 'the mass of
     this cell' and -1.67% for 'the mass on this field'.
